    DRIFT IS REFUSED ON BOTH OF ITS CLAIMS. It predicts -0.034 in the
    learning arm and that the learning arm decays MOST. Measured:
    +0.016 +/- 0.013, which is 3.9 SE off the prediction, and the
    learning arm is the arm that decays LEAST -- the only one that
    rises, with every control falling below it. The gap NARROWS, where
    drift requires it to widen. With own voice refused by
    intervention and gate corruption refused at the wrong sign
    (+0.72), ALL THREE named causes of the -0.056 gap are dead. The
    gap is real at 6.0 SE and UNEXPLAINED -- record it that way
    rather than reaching for a fourth guess. A decay smaller than
    0.023 is still not excluded, so what dies is drift AT THE SIZE IT
    PREDICTED, not every conceivable drift.

