    POWER  a full closure moves this by 0.056; 3 x SE = 0.045  -> CAN DETECT ONE
    OWN VOICE IS REFUSED, AND THE GAP WIDENS WITHOUT IT. The test
    had the power to see a closure (3 x SE = 0.045 against the
    0.056 one would move) and the gap went the OTHER WAY instead:
    -0.037 +/- 0.015 (2.4 SE). So the creature hearing itself is not
    why its index degrades when the target tracks the word -- and
    DRIFT survives as the remaining hypothesis (MacQueen's 1/wins
    freezing prototypes under a voice that is still moving).
    WHERE THE WIDENING COMES FROM: deafening moves the CONTROL arm
    +0.030 +/- 0.004 and the TRACKING arm -0.007 +/- 0.015. Own voice is
    NOISE in the control arm, where the voice is word-independent,
    and roughly NEUTRAL in the tracking arm, where it is
    word-correlated -- and under the default kWords table `heard` is
    echo-ALIGNED (targets-fight-the-echo is regime-specific), so
    there the own voice REINFORCES the caregiver's word and cutting
    it removes signal along with the noise. At this n the widening
    is under the 3 SE bar: suggestive, not established.

